WEBVTT

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.450
Wind Ensemble Competition

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.930
Hurry!

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.680
I'm so nervous.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:48.510
Here we go!

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:55.010
Gold!

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:56.420
We got gold!

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:58.830
I'm going to go tell Asami.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.310
She couldn't bring herself to come inside,
so she's hiding in the washroom.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.600
The following schools will be
moving on to the Kansai Competition.

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:14.480
Gold...

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.750
We only got dud gold,
but it's still a gold.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:28.210
Kousaka-san?

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:31.000
Moved to tears of joy, huh?

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.590
Congratulations, we got gold.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.010
I hate this.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.930
I hate this so much, I want to die.

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:45.730
How can everyone be this happy
when we didn't qualify?

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:49.260
Weren't we trying to make it
all the way to nationals?

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.610
Did you really think
we could make nationals?

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.280
Doesn't this upset you?

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.200
Because I'm upset!

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:05.370
I'm totally upset!

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:33.400
<i>I knew I shouldn't have believed what I heard,
about how my breasts would get bigger</i>

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.380
<i>once I was in high school.</i>

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.300
I'm heading out.

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.320
Take care!

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.450
<i>When my high school life began,</i>

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:48.540
<i>things like that were all I could think about.</i>

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.300
Entrance

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.300
Ceremony

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.300
<i>Not too many people from my junior high
class chose to attend this school.</i>

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.970
<i>I chose it because it was the only one with those sailor-style uniforms that I've always liked.</i>

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:10.140
<i>And because, in a lot of ways,
I wanted a fresh start.</i>

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.080
Attention, new students!

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.020
Welcome to Kitauji High School!

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:17.230
It's the school's wind ensemble.

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:20.720
Let us welcome you with a performance!

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:52.770
They're awful.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.270
<i>They're so bad!</i>

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.440
<i>They weren't together at all.</i>

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:02.050
<i>They were out of tune
and they couldn't keep a steady pulse.</i>

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:07.280
<i>Then again, I guess
they aren't trying for nationals.</i>

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:14.690
But they were <i>terrible</i>.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:18.460
Kumiko, let's walk home together.

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.380
Huh? Kumiko?

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:23.050
Uh, isn't that your name?

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.420
Yeah, it is.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.380
Right, then!

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.240
I'm Hazuki!

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.690
You can call me Katou.

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:30.810
Either is fine with me.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:33.040
So what was terrible?

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.890
Forget I said anything.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:41.770
Hey, isn't that Tuba-kun?

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:42.670
Huh?

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.070
He's adorable.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:45.950
What's he supposed to be?

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.890
It's a tuba mascot character.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:49.780
"Tuba"?

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.620
It's a brass instrument.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.560
"Brass instrument"?

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.960
Midori was in the wind ensemble, on contrabass.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.260
"Contrabass"?

00:05:58.260 --> 00:05:59.130
Midori?

00:05:59.590 --> 00:06:02.210
Midori is my name.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:06.010
A contrabass is a string instrument this big!

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.720
It's like a giant violin.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:09.760
Have you seen one before?

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.450
I think I have!

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:12.500
That so?

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:13.900
I was in a wind ensemble, too.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.340
Really?!

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:17.390
Um...

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.420
Oh, she's Oumae Kumiko.

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:20.480
You can call her Kumiko.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.890
I'm Hazuki.

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:22.630
Nice to meet you!

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:23.560
Copy.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:24.750
What about you?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.130
What part did you play?

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:28.390
Oh, lower brass.

00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:29.780
I used to play euph.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:32.060
Yeah, I can see that.

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:33.450
Huh? UFO?

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:35.490
Not UFO, euph.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.470
It's actually called a euphonium.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:39.040
It's like a smaller tuba.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.210
Yeah?

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:43.040
I was about to go watch
the wind ensemble perform.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:46.510
How about we all go together?

00:06:49.060 --> 00:06:51.220
H-Hazuki-chan...

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.250
Are you all right?

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.800
What's this?

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.330
Are you here to watch?

00:06:57.330 --> 00:06:59.250
Well, come on in!

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.060
Come on, join us!

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.810
Bronze Prize

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.810
Kitauji Prefectural High School

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.310
Bronze Prize

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:04.320
Bronze...

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:06.230
Let's tune. Concert B-flat, everyone.

00:07:14.080 --> 00:07:15.490
Trombone, watch your slide.

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:19.790
Horn, you're a bit off. Listen carefully.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.460
Let's try that again.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:26.400
You can use your tuners.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:28.230
What happened?

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:30.130
They were a little out of tune.

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:31.670
Really?

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.310
<i>Kousaka-san?!</i>

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:46.480
Excuse me.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:48.650
Are you here to watch?

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:51.610
No, I'd like to join.

00:07:56.590 --> 00:07:58.160
Why?

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:01.460
Kousaka-san was there.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:09.090
I thought she'd be at Rakushu or Rikka or something since she's really good.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.550
This sucks.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:12.830
What's wrong?

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:16.660
'Sup?

00:08:17.480 --> 00:08:18.510
Oh, Shuuichi.

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:20.140
Huh?

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:24.000
We've known each other since we were little. At least say hi.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:26.230
We go to the same school too.

00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:29.610
Oh yeah, I saw Kousaka Reina.

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:31.430
I had no idea.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:34.320
Well, looks like someone's a bit sluggish today.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.310
Oh right!

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:37.250
I don't have time for this.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:37.970
Hey.

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:39.870
Sorry, I'm going home.

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:43.040
Hey, what are you doing as far as clubs?

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:46.380
I haven't decided yet.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.180
Not the ensemble?

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.050
What about you?

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:49.920
Me?

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:52.690
Well, it isn't like there's anything else I want to do.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:54.500
Wind ensemble it is, I guess.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.340
Oh.

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:01.520
I'm...

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:08.360
Your new advisor, Taki-sensei,
will be starting tomorrow.

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.780
If you have any other
questions, ask him then.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:14.530
Now, behave like proper high school
students and dress appropriately.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:16.990
Make sure you work hard on your club activities as well.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:18.100
That is all.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.580
I wonder what Taki-sensei is like.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.830
Okay.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.710
Let's start assigning instruments.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:32.160
My name is Ogasawara Haruka,
and I'm your club president.

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:33.980
I play the baritone sax,

00:09:33.980 --> 00:09:37.510
so if you're gonna be a part of a sax section,
you'll be seeing a lot of me.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:38.180
Now...

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:39.300
My turn!

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:41.120
Who wants to play bass?

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.180
Not yet.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:46.560
I know that some of you
are complete beginners,

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:48.850
so let's start by introducing the instruments.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:51.180
First up, trumpet.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:56.740
I'm the trumpet section leader,
Nakaseko Kaori.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:01.240
Kaori-senpai's so pretty, as always!

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:04.640
Within the brass family,
the trumpet is often the lead instrument.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.340
It plays the melody
and gets solo sections.

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.920
I'm sure you'll enjoy it.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:11.720
We have five people on trumpet right now,
and we're all good friends.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:14.070
I hope you join our section!

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:16.800
Next.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:20.720
Trombone is...

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:23.030
Among the woodwinds...

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:25.570
Its beautiful timbre...

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:28.490
It's actually pretty good for relieving stress!

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:31.480
You might have seen one on TV.

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:37.060
Bass section leader and
vice president, Tanaka Asuka!

00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:38.900
I play euph.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.550
Euph.

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:47.780
There's also an instrument called the contrabass that plays bass.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:51.250
Unfortunately, we don't have anyone playing contrabass right now.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:52.670
If anyone here...

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:55.990
Have you played contrabass before?

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:57.380
Yes, I played at Seijo.

00:10:57.960 --> 00:10:58.590
Score!

00:10:58.950 --> 00:10:59.930
Will you play?

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:02.260
I've been waiting to hear those words.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.510
I like you!

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:07.310
The fingering is similar to the recorder's.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.180
When you switch from C to D...

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:09.180
How do you hold it?

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.550
I'll be trying out the other instruments.

00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:13.060
Okay.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:25.620
That's called a reed. It's made of wood,
and it has to be replaced often,

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:25.620
And don't grip that thin,
metal part too much. Yeah, that's it.

00:11:26.850 --> 00:11:28.160
How was that?

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.840
You're so good, Kousaka-san!

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:34.180
Which middle school did you go to?

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:35.880
Kita Middle School.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:39.220
I also take private lessons.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:40.450
No wonder...

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.130
You surprised me.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:45.370
Thank you for your praise.

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:46.600
I'm delighted to hear it.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:50.100
<i>We decided on our instruments. I'm on euph.</i>

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.260
<i>Hazuki-chan is on tuba.</i>

00:11:52.260 --> 00:11:55.860
<i>Midori-chan is on contrabass.</i>

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:05.410
<i>Our bass section includes Asuka-senpai and three second-year members.</i>

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:11.620
I'll take this one!

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:13.250
That was fast.

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:15.160
Yes, our eyes locked.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:16.750
It has eyes?!

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:17.960
I'll call it...

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.200
George-kun!

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:20.090
I think.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.120
George?

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:21.670
Yes.

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:28.180
The euphs are here.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.600
Okay, um...

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:31.470
There are two, huh?

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:33.390
Plenty to choose from, right?

00:12:34.970 --> 00:12:37.980
<i>There are so many other instruments left.</i>

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.360
I recommend this.

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:44.010
The fourth valve is placed lower on this one, so it's easier to play.

00:12:44.010 --> 00:12:45.780
It's a bit old, but...

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:48.760
Here.

00:12:51.960 --> 00:12:53.910
Yeah, it's nice.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:58.130
No one played it last year,
so I bet it's dying to be played.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:03.670
I'll take this one.

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:10.770
I will be the wind ensemble advisor. My name is Taki Noboru.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.270
Pleased to meet you all.

00:13:13.890 --> 00:13:15.850
He's pretty hot, isn't he?

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:16.770
You think so?

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:19.720
We got twenty-two new members?

00:13:19.720 --> 00:13:22.360
That'll make filling in missing parts easy.

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:27.610
Now, before we begin,
I have a few things to say.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:32.240
My philosophy is to value
a student's sense of initiative.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:36.210
Therefore, as your advisor this year, I...

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.780
Oh, sorry.

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:41.250
I would like you all
to set a goal for the year.

00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:46.400
This was your goal last year, correct?

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:51.260
We <i>did</i> try, but...

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.390
Um... Excuse me,

00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:01.230
but I don't think that was
meant to be a realistic goal.

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:03.170
I see.

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.150
Let's just scratch this, then.

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:10.580
So please, decide on a goal.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.490
I'll go along with whatever you choose.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.150
Decide?

00:14:14.150 --> 00:14:16.180
Yes, decide.

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:20.910
If you want to go for nationals,
your rehearsals will be more focused.

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:24.980
On the other hand, if you just
want to make good memories,

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:27.050
we don't need to
work ourselves too hard.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:30.820
Personally, I believe either is fine.

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:32.930
Please decide for yourselves.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.470
You want <i>us</i> to decide?

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:37.230
I believe that's what I said.

00:14:40.870 --> 00:14:41.940
All right.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:44.750
Let's vote on it. I'll tally it up.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:45.780
A vote?

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:47.860
<i>Crap, what do I do?</i>

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:54.160
Um... Okay, who wants to make competing in nationals our goal for the year?

00:14:57.610 --> 00:14:58.250
<i>What...</i>

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.000
<i>do I do?</i>

00:15:02.890 --> 00:15:08.640
Based on the vote, we'll be working
toward the national competition.

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:09.730
Thank you.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:16.050
Even though it wasn't unanimous,
you chose your goal yourselves.

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:19.280
I'll do everything I can
to help you reach that goal,

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:21.620
but it's up to you
to put in the work.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.850
Please don't forget that.

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:24.980
Okay, everyone?

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:25.830
Yes.

00:15:26.920 --> 00:15:29.650
Don't just stand there.
I need an answer.

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:31.280
Yes.

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:33.720
I'll ask again.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.530
Okay, everyone?

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:36.760
Yes.

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:41.620
Sunrise Festival?

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.360
Yeah, or SunFes for short.

00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:45.210
It's a pretty big deal around here.

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:49.570
The wind ensembles from
various schools play in a march.

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:51.780
Can we really pull that off?

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:55.300
Since you're new, you might be doing steps, Hazuki-chan.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:58.930
Sax-kun!

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.730
Didn't get it again, huh?

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.110
Okay, everyone.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.470
Are you ready?

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:12.720
This is going to be our first real rehearsal.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:14.240
I'm looking forward to working with you.

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:18.910
Well then, let's run it from the top.

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:23.210
Three, four...

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:44.270
That's enough.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.150
What is this?

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:54.210
President, didn't I say to come get me

00:16:54.210 --> 00:16:57.230
once you're good enough
to play as an ensemble?

00:16:57.230 --> 00:16:58.450
Yes.

00:16:58.450 --> 00:17:00.510
So you think this is good enough?

00:17:01.690 --> 00:17:02.910
I'm sorry.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:06.450
You decided that we're going for nationals.

00:17:06.450 --> 00:17:11.090
So you need to get your playing at
a minimum standard during sectionals.

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:14.760
The way you're playing now,
you're not even ready for my instruction.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:17.750
Please don't waste my time.

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:19.280
President.

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:19.930
Yes?

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.970
That'll be it for today.

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:24.850
We'll make some time next Wednesday to practice as an ensemble.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:26.290
That is all.

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:29.220
U-Um...

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:30.450
What is it?

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:32.650
What do we play for the Sunrise Festival?

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:36.420
You aren't at the point where
you can be thinking about that yet.

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:38.740
If you can't play properly by next week,

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:41.580
you should probably
reconsider participating.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:42.350
Excuse me.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:48.000
What's his problem?

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.030
He finally comes by and all he tells us is that we shouldn't play in SunFes?

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:54.710
Does he seriously want us to
practice this piece for another week?

00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.180
It's canceled?

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:04.430
We thought about
practicing on our own, but...

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:07.100
Some people thought
there'd be no point in that.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:12.560
So practice is canceled until the
section leaders' meeting is over.

00:18:12.560 --> 00:18:13.650
I'm really sorry!

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:20.740
<i>According to the president,
some students started saying</i>

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:24.910
<i>that they wouldn't practice until
we decide what to do about our conductor.</i>

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:32.880
<i>We first-years had no choice but to go along.</i>

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.140
Who's that?

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:40.370
It's Kousaka-san.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:40.930
Huh?

00:18:41.940 --> 00:18:43.520
It's Kousaka-san.

00:19:16.860 --> 00:19:18.330
This is...

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:19.810
It's "From the New World."

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:24.180
I heard Dvořák wrote it while he was in the United States,

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:28.290
thinking about his homeland of Bohemia.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:39.100
In a barren, brand-new world...

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.820
<i>Regular practices resumed the following day.</i>

00:20:15.820 --> 00:20:16.720
Wait up!

00:20:16.720 --> 00:20:18.000
I have to talk to you.

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:18.650
What?

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:20.920
It's about Kousaka.

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:22.260
Did Kousaka-san do something wrong?

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:23.100
No!

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:26.660
The seniors in the trumpet
section have their eye on her.

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:31.290
<i>Yes. In terms of practice time,
about half of what I had in middle school.</i>

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:36.070
Taki-sensei asked her a question, and she spoke her mind.

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:37.210
I see.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:47.200
A good teacher would have her back.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:51.860
But apparently, this is his first
time advising a wind ensemble.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:53.230
Really?

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:56.340
He keeps making us
repeat the same exercises,

00:20:56.340 --> 00:20:58.080
and he's pretty heavy-handed.

00:20:58.080 --> 00:20:59.950
I mean, he <i>does</i> have a talent for teaching—

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:01.650
Of course he does.

00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:03.740
Kousaka!

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.590
Why are you here?

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:07.570
I live near here.

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:09.460
I've never seen you.

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:11.410
Probably because
I don't take the train.

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:13.410
I bike to and from school.

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:16.910
Just so you know,
Taki-sensei's awesome.

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:18.710
I won't let you say
bad things about him!

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.250
O-Okay.

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:22.050
Got it?

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:23.880
Got it.

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:27.930
I wasn't saying anything bad—

00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:28.850
Did you say something?

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:31.260
No, nothing!

00:21:40.840 --> 00:21:41.900
We're running?

00:21:42.270 --> 00:21:43.030
Correct.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:45.260
Do a lap around the
field as fast as you can.

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:46.820
You have ninety seconds to complete it.

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:49.320
Anyone that takes longer
will be doing another lap.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:49.810
Huh?

00:21:49.810 --> 00:21:52.080
Excuse me, what's the point of that?

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.750
Ready? Go!

00:21:56.710 --> 00:22:01.730
<i>If we couldn't meet Taki-sensei's standards by next week's ensemble,</i>

00:22:01.730 --> 00:22:03.800
<i>we would withdraw from SunFes.</i>

00:22:04.450 --> 00:22:09.680
<i>The only way to play at SunFes was to follow his direction.</i>

00:22:14.810 --> 00:22:19.770
<i>Steamed up by Taki-sensei's admonitions and fanned on by the atmosphere within the club,</i>

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:23.990
<i>we continued practicing for the coming ensemble.</i>

00:22:25.420 --> 00:22:27.820
I just don't get that teacher!

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:31.450
Personally, I don't hate the way he does things.

00:22:31.840 --> 00:22:34.720
I think we're in trouble for SunFes.

00:22:36.350 --> 00:22:37.620
I got it!

00:22:45.940 --> 00:22:46.420
All right.

00:22:46.810 --> 00:22:47.870
Let's go practice our piece!

00:22:47.870 --> 00:22:48.690
Okay!

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:53.480
<i>After he rejected everything about the way we used to do things,</i>

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:56.350
<i>there was a lot of resentment
toward Taki-sensei.</i>

00:22:56.940 --> 00:23:02.060
<i>But that frustration became
a unifying force for the band members.</i>

00:23:03.620 --> 00:23:06.650
<i>And on the day of that rehearsal...</i>

00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:08.900
I'm not letting him complain!

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:11.110
If he does, I'm <i>so</i> throwing
my mouthpiece at him.

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:14.510
And why doesn't he use a baton?

00:23:14.510 --> 00:23:15.950
I can't tell where his ictuses are.

00:23:29.610 --> 00:23:31.440
Today's the day.

00:23:32.290 --> 00:23:34.830
I'm eager to see what you've
accomplished in this past week.

00:23:35.710 --> 00:23:37.520
Torizuka-san, please.

00:23:54.510 --> 00:23:55.880
Are you all ready?

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:57.680
Well then...

00:23:59.180 --> 00:24:00.270
Let's begin.

00:24:02.350 --> 00:24:03.040
Three...

00:25:18.580 --> 00:25:19.450
Very well.

00:25:20.060 --> 00:25:23.790
There were a lot of things I could nitpick,

00:25:24.230 --> 00:25:25.290
but all in all,

00:25:25.860 --> 00:25:29.150
<i>that was an ensemble.</i>

00:25:32.580 --> 00:25:36.010
Ogasawara-san, could you
please hand this out to everyone?

00:25:36.010 --> 00:25:36.770
Yes.

00:25:39.750 --> 00:25:42.470
Now, everyone,
here's what you've been waiting for.

00:25:43.180 --> 00:25:45.560
It's the practice schedule for SunFes.

00:25:45.560 --> 00:25:47.450
Are we seriously going to do all this?!

00:25:47.450 --> 00:25:49.020
Even on Sundays?!

00:25:49.320 --> 00:25:52.930
Now, we don't have that many days left.

00:25:52.930 --> 00:25:58.400
But if you sacrifice the time
you all waste being young,

00:25:58.400 --> 00:26:00.530
this much practice
shouldn't be that difficult.

00:26:00.530 --> 00:26:01.870
I <i>still</i> don't like him.

00:26:02.140 --> 00:26:04.810
SunFes is fun,

00:26:04.810 --> 00:26:09.040
but it's also an important event where talented schools gather in a non-competitive environment.

00:26:09.410 --> 00:26:14.170
We'll take this opportunity to show them
that Kitauji is different this year.

00:26:14.170 --> 00:26:16.280
But it's already too late.

00:26:16.280 --> 00:26:17.870
Do you think we can't?

00:26:19.210 --> 00:26:21.440
I believe we can.

00:26:21.440 --> 00:26:26.890
We're going for nationals, after all.

00:26:29.290 --> 00:26:32.150
<i>Seeing his defiant and unwavering smile,</i>

00:26:32.580 --> 00:26:35.070
<i>we all realized</i>

00:26:35.420 --> 00:26:38.110
<i>that our teacher was dead serious.</i>

00:26:41.120 --> 00:26:43.540
Keep your feet together.

00:26:43.540 --> 00:26:44.950
You're teetering a little.

00:26:44.950 --> 00:26:46.160
Look straight ahead.

00:26:46.920 --> 00:26:48.650
Stand straight and tall.

00:26:48.650 --> 00:26:51.250
You there, you're not together with us.

00:26:52.090 --> 00:26:54.210
<i>From the day we played
"Marines' Hymn" as an ensemble,</i>

00:26:54.560 --> 00:26:57.220
<i>the club's overall mindset
had noticeably changed.</i>

00:26:58.350 --> 00:27:00.800
<i>We went from "It won't matter how hard we try,"</i>

00:27:00.800 --> 00:27:03.600
<i>to "We'll improve if we work hard."</i>

00:27:04.700 --> 00:27:06.100
<i>People aren't complicated.</i>

00:27:06.840 --> 00:27:09.970
<i>We work hard when we know that
we'll get something in return,</i>

00:27:09.970 --> 00:27:13.060
<i>and we try to work even harder if that something is our own improvement.</i>

00:27:18.970 --> 00:27:21.980
<i>On the day of a wind ensemble event or performance,</i>

00:27:21.980 --> 00:27:23.620
<i>we start with a very busy morning.</i>

00:27:24.350 --> 00:27:26.410
<i>First, it goes without saying</i>

00:27:26.410 --> 00:27:29.170
<i>that we have to transport our instruments to the venue.</i>

00:27:29.170 --> 00:27:31.960
<i>We can carry the smaller instruments by hand,</i>

00:27:31.960 --> 00:27:36.550
<i>but the bigger instruments are brought by truck.</i>

00:27:36.550 --> 00:27:40.170
<i>We pack them into the truck according to
how the people in charge of moving want it done.</i>

00:27:40.170 --> 00:27:42.180
<i>It takes a lot of heavy lifting.</i>

00:27:42.180 --> 00:27:45.810
<i>The guys in the ensemble are really useful at times like this.</i>

00:27:49.600 --> 00:27:50.230
Are you okay?

00:27:51.620 --> 00:27:52.230
Yeah.

00:27:52.230 --> 00:27:53.650
I got it.

00:28:06.300 --> 00:28:07.660
Attention, everyone.

00:28:07.660 --> 00:28:09.000
This is the real deal.

00:28:09.300 --> 00:28:11.140
Don't you dare let yourselves slack one bit!

00:28:11.140 --> 00:28:11.830
Yes.

00:28:11.830 --> 00:28:13.670
Do it as you practiced, and you'll succeed!

00:28:13.670 --> 00:28:14.210
Yes!

00:28:14.460 --> 00:28:16.630
Come on, I can't hear you!

00:28:16.630 --> 00:28:17.690
Yes!

00:28:25.400 --> 00:28:27.070
Kumiko-chan.

00:28:27.880 --> 00:28:29.590
It's Rikka.

00:28:30.390 --> 00:28:32.810
Rikka? <i>The</i> Rikka High School?

00:28:32.810 --> 00:28:33.810
Yes.

00:28:33.810 --> 00:28:36.640
They're ridiculously good at marching.

00:28:36.640 --> 00:28:41.030
With their unique choreography,
they're called the light-blue demons.

00:28:41.030 --> 00:28:42.820
They're so cute.

00:28:42.820 --> 00:28:47.890
Right from the start, they're performing
and prancing around with smiles on their faces.

00:28:47.890 --> 00:28:50.480
They really are scary.

00:28:50.480 --> 00:28:51.570
Seriously?

00:28:51.570 --> 00:28:54.170
Oh, in the program...

00:28:55.980 --> 00:28:59.340
I knew it! It's Rikka, then us, then Rakushu!

00:29:00.490 --> 00:29:02.670
So what does that mean?

00:29:02.670 --> 00:29:04.010
It's the worst situation.

00:29:04.280 --> 00:29:07.470
We'll probably be overshadowed by them.
There's a chance we'll be completely blotted out.

00:29:08.320 --> 00:29:10.520
Huh? That sucks!

00:29:10.810 --> 00:29:12.350
Kumiko!

00:29:12.350 --> 00:29:13.160
Huh?

00:29:13.160 --> 00:29:14.160
Azusa-chan?

00:29:14.160 --> 00:29:15.020
Do you know her?

00:29:15.020 --> 00:29:18.230
Yeah, in middle school,
we were in wind ensemble together.

00:29:18.230 --> 00:29:21.150
We still have some time, right? I'll be over there.

00:29:22.030 --> 00:29:24.210
I didn't know you were in Kitauji.

00:29:24.210 --> 00:29:27.280
You went to Rikka, huh, Azusa-chan?

00:29:27.280 --> 00:29:29.110
I wanted to wear this outfit.

00:29:29.110 --> 00:29:31.910
It's pretty hardcore, but nothing I didn't expect.

00:29:31.910 --> 00:29:33.500
Well, yeah, it's Rikka.

00:29:33.500 --> 00:29:36.150
So why are you at Kitauji?

00:29:36.150 --> 00:29:36.850
Huh?

00:29:36.850 --> 00:29:38.240
There must be a reason.

00:29:38.240 --> 00:29:39.750
Is that where your friends went?

00:29:39.750 --> 00:29:42.920
Oh, yeah! Kitauji is where Kousaka Reina—

00:29:42.920 --> 00:29:47.140
I heard she declined Rikka's invitation to go to Kitauji.

00:29:47.140 --> 00:29:49.550
Wh-What?! Really?

00:29:49.550 --> 00:29:52.450
We were all saying there must have been a reason.

00:29:52.450 --> 00:29:54.580
Like, a lot of hot guys go there or something.

00:29:55.560 --> 00:29:56.440
Maybe not.

00:29:56.440 --> 00:29:58.340
Has she told you, Kumiko?

00:29:58.340 --> 00:30:01.000
Like, what's there at Kitauji?

00:30:01.000 --> 00:30:01.940
I don't know!

00:30:01.940 --> 00:30:03.280
There isn't anything special.

00:30:03.280 --> 00:30:05.680
Come on, tell me!

00:30:05.680 --> 00:30:07.490
Sorry, hang on.

00:30:08.230 --> 00:30:10.300
Minamiuji just arrived.

00:30:10.300 --> 00:30:11.730
Let's go meet them.

00:30:11.730 --> 00:30:13.620
The parking lot's right over there.

00:30:13.620 --> 00:30:17.280
Most of the people from
our middle school went to Minamiuji.

00:30:17.280 --> 00:30:18.580
I bet everyone's there!

00:30:18.580 --> 00:30:19.150
I...

00:30:19.150 --> 00:30:20.420
Come on, let's go.

00:30:20.420 --> 00:30:22.750
I haven't seen Asami and Yoko in forever!

00:30:25.050 --> 00:30:26.290
What's wrong?

00:30:35.310 --> 00:30:36.590
Hey, let's go.

00:30:38.050 --> 00:30:40.400
Sorry, I think I'll pass.

00:30:40.400 --> 00:30:41.730
Why's that?

00:30:42.060 --> 00:30:46.820
I didn't choose Kitauji because of the school itself.

00:30:47.650 --> 00:30:49.490
I just wanted a new start.

00:30:49.490 --> 00:30:52.200
Going to a high school where
I didn't know too many people...

00:30:52.200 --> 00:30:54.540
Starting fresh, from scratch.

00:30:56.470 --> 00:30:57.960
That's all.

00:30:59.650 --> 00:31:00.370
Kumiko...

00:31:01.970 --> 00:31:03.540
I see.

00:31:03.540 --> 00:31:05.630
So did you get that new start?

00:31:06.370 --> 00:31:11.040
We will now begin the Sunrise Festival,

00:31:11.040 --> 00:31:14.020
held by high school wind ensembles
across the prefecture.

00:31:13.430 --> 00:31:14.720
Time to go.

00:31:14.720 --> 00:31:15.620
Okay.

00:31:15.620 --> 00:31:18.200
I guess the next time we meet will be at the competition.

00:31:18.200 --> 00:31:19.410
I guess so.

00:31:19.410 --> 00:31:20.490
Good luck to both of us.

00:31:20.490 --> 00:31:21.950
Yeah, see you.

00:31:24.770 --> 00:31:29.110
<i>That's when I realized I had the new start I wanted,</i>

00:31:29.650 --> 00:31:33.200
<i>and that I wasn't regretting it one bit.</i>

00:31:40.070 --> 00:31:44.210
<i>Next, we have the Rikka High School Wind Ensemble.</i>

00:31:48.570 --> 00:31:51.130
What is this? This is insane.

00:31:51.130 --> 00:31:53.390
It's Rikka High School's party favorite.

00:31:57.430 --> 00:31:58.520
They're coming.

00:32:00.950 --> 00:32:02.050
They're way too good.

00:32:02.050 --> 00:32:02.980
Right?

00:32:02.980 --> 00:32:04.710
They haven't missed a beat.

00:32:04.710 --> 00:32:06.480
This is going to be tragic for us.

00:32:06.480 --> 00:32:08.100
Take a deep breath.

00:32:08.100 --> 00:32:09.110
Okay.

00:32:09.110 --> 00:32:12.340
I'm not feeling so confident anymore.

00:32:12.340 --> 00:32:14.120
It's okay, stay calm.

00:32:14.120 --> 00:32:16.530
Hey, we're almost up.

00:32:16.530 --> 00:32:17.370
Get a grip, every—

00:32:27.080 --> 00:32:29.740
You idiot, why are you making all that noise, Kousaka?

00:32:29.740 --> 00:32:32.720
Didn't they tell us we're supposed to stay quiet while we're here?

00:32:32.720 --> 00:32:33.970
Sorry.

00:32:41.640 --> 00:32:45.520
<i>Next, Kitauji High School Wind Ensemble.</i>

00:32:45.920 --> 00:32:53.030
Music isn't supposed to be something
you do to show off your abilities to your rivals.

00:32:53.530 --> 00:32:57.880
But all these spectators and students of other schools

00:32:57.880 --> 00:33:00.450
still don't know what Kitauji is capable of.

00:33:00.770 --> 00:33:05.170
So I believe today is a good opportunity for them to learn.

00:33:06.460 --> 00:33:10.800
Now, go show them what Kitauji is made of.

00:33:12.890 --> 00:33:13.670
Yes!

00:34:00.930 --> 00:34:01.810
Huh?

00:34:01.810 --> 00:34:02.890
They're awesome.

00:34:02.890 --> 00:34:04.210
They're pretty good.

00:34:04.210 --> 00:34:05.390
Which school was this again?

00:34:07.940 --> 00:34:09.610
Not bad.

00:34:09.610 --> 00:34:12.440
Did you see the drum major? She's beautiful!

00:34:12.440 --> 00:34:13.930
Do you know who this is?

00:34:13.930 --> 00:34:15.700
No, lemme take a look.

00:35:37.630 --> 00:35:42.960
<i>With SunFes past, we began practice for the summer competition.</i>

00:35:42.960 --> 00:35:46.500
I've handed out our schedule
for the upcoming weeks.

00:35:47.880 --> 00:35:50.960
Now this is the important part:

00:35:51.960 --> 00:35:54.880
This year, I would like to hold auditions.

00:35:56.200 --> 00:35:57.760
Auditions?

00:35:57.760 --> 00:35:58.380
Yes.

00:35:58.380 --> 00:36:02.760
I will listen to each of you play, then choose

00:36:03.100 --> 00:36:06.910
the members and chair order for the competition.

00:36:10.060 --> 00:36:13.690
I got the sheets and CDs for the required
repertoire choice and the free-choice piece.

00:36:14.160 --> 00:36:17.150
Tasaka Naoki's "Wind of Provence" from the required repertoire list,

00:36:17.150 --> 00:36:20.160
and Horikawa Namie's "Crescent Moon Dance"
for our free-choice piece.

00:36:20.160 --> 00:36:22.780
Taki-sensei knows what's up!

00:36:28.220 --> 00:36:29.520
This is pretty great!

00:36:29.520 --> 00:36:30.670
I know, right?

00:36:31.440 --> 00:36:34.040
The bass parts in this piece are so nice.

00:36:35.300 --> 00:36:38.300
<i>The piece was certainly dynamic.</i>

00:36:38.300 --> 00:36:41.390
<i>But if we didn't have it down pat,
it would sound terrible.</i>

00:36:42.430 --> 00:36:44.240
<i>That's when I realized...</i>

00:36:44.240 --> 00:36:48.330
<i>Taki-sensei was definitely aiming for nationals.</i>

00:36:58.150 --> 00:36:59.070
What do you think?

00:37:02.570 --> 00:37:04.880
There are three first-years playing trombone, right?

00:37:04.880 --> 00:37:06.910
Yeah. Me, Fukui, and Akamatsu.

00:37:06.910 --> 00:37:09.370
I bet all the euphs will make it.

00:37:09.370 --> 00:37:11.040
Well, there aren't too many of us.

00:37:11.040 --> 00:37:15.700
But I have a feeling Taki-sensei wouldn't hesitate
to drop the whole section if we aren't good enough.

00:37:15.700 --> 00:37:17.130
I can't let myself relax.

00:37:17.460 --> 00:37:20.380
Could you imagine if we actually made nationals?

00:37:21.040 --> 00:37:24.110
It's only been two months
since I joined the wind ensemble,

00:37:24.110 --> 00:37:26.050
but I'm starting to think
it might just be possible.

00:37:26.050 --> 00:37:27.860
Easier said than done.

00:37:27.860 --> 00:37:30.470
Yeah, but we've improved a ton already.

00:37:32.110 --> 00:37:35.930
I want to get even better.

00:37:36.680 --> 00:37:39.730
Hey, let's practice here together next time.

00:37:39.730 --> 00:37:42.050
Nah, my euphonium's too heavy.

00:37:42.050 --> 00:37:42.860
Fine, whatever.

00:37:45.800 --> 00:37:48.620
What are you doing June 5th?

00:37:48.620 --> 00:37:49.920
The 5th?

00:37:49.920 --> 00:37:50.950
Just band, as usual.

00:37:51.500 --> 00:37:52.790
After that!

00:37:53.270 --> 00:37:54.430
The Agata Festival.

00:37:55.110 --> 00:37:56.330
Do you want to go with me?

00:37:57.430 --> 00:37:59.040
Huh? Why?

00:38:01.170 --> 00:38:03.210
Just give it some thought.

00:38:04.800 --> 00:38:05.630
Later.

00:38:06.470 --> 00:38:09.510
<i>He took me completely by surprise.</i>

00:38:09.510 --> 00:38:13.940
<i>My thoughts became a scattered mess.</i>

00:38:13.940 --> 00:38:15.140
What the...

00:38:16.940 --> 00:38:18.640
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:38:19.900 --> 00:38:20.820
<i>Uh oh.</i>

00:38:23.820 --> 00:38:26.320
Sorry, Akamatsu, I gotta go.

00:38:33.100 --> 00:38:34.410
All right, let's do this.

00:38:40.610 --> 00:38:41.670
It's you.

00:38:41.670 --> 00:38:42.380
What?

00:38:42.380 --> 00:38:43.560
"What" yourself.

00:38:43.560 --> 00:38:44.780
You just gave me the signal.

00:38:44.780 --> 00:38:46.520
Me? No, I didn't.

00:38:46.520 --> 00:38:47.500
Yeah, you did.

00:38:47.500 --> 00:38:49.240
You looked at me and then went out by yourself.

00:38:49.240 --> 00:38:51.720
How is <i>that</i> a signal?

00:38:51.720 --> 00:38:53.760
You'd think it was if you were me.

00:38:53.760 --> 00:38:55.060
Anyway, the Agata Festival—

00:38:55.060 --> 00:38:57.080
Oh, that.

00:39:00.490 --> 00:39:01.560
Did you have other plans?

00:39:03.250 --> 00:39:06.320
Sorry, I'm going to go with this person.

00:39:06.320 --> 00:39:08.490
Huh? With Kousaka?

00:39:11.120 --> 00:39:12.490
Tsukamoto.

00:39:20.380 --> 00:39:22.710
Can I talk to you for a second?

00:39:23.450 --> 00:39:24.850
I'm talking to Kumiko right now.

00:39:24.850 --> 00:39:26.170
Go talk to her!

00:39:26.170 --> 00:39:27.970
Go talk to her, Shuichi.

00:39:29.760 --> 00:39:31.050
Is that what you want?

00:39:31.640 --> 00:39:32.300
Yeah.

00:39:34.750 --> 00:39:35.470
Fine.

00:40:03.590 --> 00:40:04.880
Katou!

00:40:05.300 --> 00:40:06.770
Sorry I'm late.

00:40:07.560 --> 00:40:08.300
'Sup?

00:40:15.100 --> 00:40:16.470
Why?

00:40:16.470 --> 00:40:20.500
Why do I have to bring my euphonium?

00:40:20.500 --> 00:40:21.970
You're ten minutes late.

00:40:23.320 --> 00:40:24.150
Huh?

00:40:26.230 --> 00:40:27.070
What?

00:40:27.070 --> 00:40:29.990
Nothing. I was just surprised by how cute you look.

00:40:32.890 --> 00:40:33.570
Let's go.

00:40:33.570 --> 00:40:35.600
Go where?

00:40:35.600 --> 00:40:36.370
Mt. Daikichi.

00:40:36.720 --> 00:40:37.700
It's a short hike.

00:40:40.920 --> 00:40:42.540
Finally, a chance to sit down.

00:40:42.540 --> 00:40:44.280
Here, have some takoyaki.

00:40:44.280 --> 00:40:45.840
They've gone a bit cold, though.

00:40:45.840 --> 00:40:46.760
Thanks.

00:40:47.400 --> 00:40:50.210
This is my first time going to
the Agata Festival with a guy.

00:40:50.210 --> 00:40:51.770
Yeah, likewise.

00:40:51.770 --> 00:40:53.970
I'm not really used to this kind of thing.

00:40:55.210 --> 00:40:57.830
Hey, Katou, is your tuba playing coming along well?

00:40:57.830 --> 00:40:59.260
Didn't you take it home the other day?

00:40:59.260 --> 00:41:01.380
Tsukamoto, you know...

00:41:01.380 --> 00:41:03.480
I like you.

00:41:07.430 --> 00:41:09.980
Sure. Uh, yeah.

00:41:10.570 --> 00:41:12.290
What's with that reaction?

00:41:12.290 --> 00:41:13.780
Nothing, you just surprised me.

00:41:15.490 --> 00:41:17.010
So, what's your response?

00:41:27.740 --> 00:41:28.530
Sorry.

00:41:36.530 --> 00:41:37.470
Oh.

00:41:43.380 --> 00:41:46.940
To be honest, I've been thinking about it lately.

00:41:47.720 --> 00:41:49.860
I've been wanting to hang out with you.

00:41:49.860 --> 00:41:50.630
Huh?

00:41:53.170 --> 00:41:55.110
You know how you have a terrible personality?

00:41:56.610 --> 00:41:58.750
How am I supposed to take that?

00:41:58.750 --> 00:41:59.910
It's a compliment.

00:42:00.410 --> 00:42:02.680
At that competition,

00:42:02.680 --> 00:42:06.080
you asked if I really thought
we could make nationals.

00:42:06.080 --> 00:42:08.040
That's a terrible thing to say.

00:42:08.040 --> 00:42:11.700
No, I really did think it was a weird thought.

00:42:11.700 --> 00:42:13.520
And wait, you <i>are</i> insulting me.

00:42:13.520 --> 00:42:14.340
No.

00:42:14.760 --> 00:42:17.010
It's a confession of love.

00:42:18.230 --> 00:42:21.180
There's no way you're serious.

00:42:21.180 --> 00:42:25.390
That side of you has always interested me.

00:42:25.390 --> 00:42:28.230
It's like you wear a friendly,

00:42:28.770 --> 00:42:30.980
good-girl mask, but beneath that,

00:42:30.980 --> 00:42:33.070
you're actually really distant.

00:42:33.750 --> 00:42:37.490
It makes me want to rip that
good-girl disguise right off of you.

00:42:37.490 --> 00:42:40.030
What's that supposed to mean?

00:42:40.550 --> 00:42:43.620
Don't you understand my love?

00:42:43.620 --> 00:42:45.790
You're a weirdo, Kousaka-san.

00:42:47.750 --> 00:42:48.870
We're here.

00:42:57.010 --> 00:42:58.200
It's pretty.

00:43:00.890 --> 00:43:01.550
Yeah.

00:43:03.330 --> 00:43:06.170
So this is what you wanted to see, Kousaka-san?

00:43:07.010 --> 00:43:10.390
It's not exactly that I wanted to see it.

00:43:11.440 --> 00:43:14.110
I simply wanted to do something that others wouldn't.

00:43:15.620 --> 00:43:17.780
It's like a sea of stars!

00:43:20.930 --> 00:43:23.010
Are those the lights from the festival?

00:43:23.790 --> 00:43:25.750
Are you <i>that</i> worried about Tsukamoto?

00:43:25.750 --> 00:43:26.510
Huh?

00:43:26.510 --> 00:43:27.920
Of course not!

00:43:27.920 --> 00:43:29.750
It's not like that, anyway.

00:43:32.410 --> 00:43:34.290
It's not, huh?

00:43:34.290 --> 00:43:35.370
No.

00:43:36.360 --> 00:43:40.220
No one else would be crazy enough to hike up

00:43:40.690 --> 00:43:42.670
a mountain on a festival day, right?

00:43:45.750 --> 00:43:48.110
I guess not.

00:43:48.110 --> 00:43:51.010
I had a feeling you'd understand.

00:43:52.440 --> 00:43:57.140
I don't try to get close to people who don't interest me.

00:43:57.140 --> 00:44:00.200
Being relieved to know
you're the same as someone else is stupid.

00:44:01.090 --> 00:44:05.300
Becoming a faceless member of
the crowd is something I want to avoid.

00:44:05.300 --> 00:44:08.910
Sometimes it's unavoidable, but...
You kind of get it, right?

00:44:08.910 --> 00:44:11.620
That sort of crazy feeling.

00:44:13.960 --> 00:44:15.540
Yeah, I get it.

00:44:15.990 --> 00:44:18.380
I know how you feel, Kousaka-san.

00:44:19.940 --> 00:44:20.840
Reina.

00:44:22.630 --> 00:44:23.870
Reina.

00:44:26.100 --> 00:44:29.060
I want to become special.

00:44:30.810 --> 00:44:33.770
I don't want to be just like everyone else.

00:44:39.390 --> 00:44:42.360
That's why I play the trumpet.

00:44:42.860 --> 00:44:44.420
To become special.

00:44:44.910 --> 00:44:47.320
<i>I was about to be completely pulled in.</i>

00:44:47.320 --> 00:44:52.210
<i>At that moment, I felt like dying by her hand wouldn't be that bad.</i>

00:44:55.490 --> 00:44:58.050
Can you become special playing the trumpet?

00:44:58.340 --> 00:44:59.510
I can.

00:44:59.510 --> 00:45:03.260
If I practice more and keep improving, I can become even more special.

00:45:03.660 --> 00:45:06.600
Not just someone who <i>thinks</i> they're special, either.

00:45:07.100 --> 00:45:08.970
I'm going to <i>truly</i> become special.

00:45:18.840 --> 00:45:21.180
You definitely have a terrible personality, Kumiko.

00:45:28.480 --> 00:45:29.700
Are you ready?

00:45:30.250 --> 00:45:31.330
Yeah, I am.

00:45:31.330 --> 00:45:32.450
What are we playing?

00:45:32.450 --> 00:45:34.020
The one we played in our third year of middle school.

00:45:34.020 --> 00:45:34.960
At the farewell party.

00:45:35.250 --> 00:45:36.050
Why that one?

00:45:40.160 --> 00:45:41.050
I like it.

00:45:43.480 --> 00:45:44.640
All right.

00:47:51.130 --> 00:47:53.260
Wow, that sounds great.

00:47:53.260 --> 00:47:55.680
Your high notes are getting really solid.

00:47:55.680 --> 00:47:56.720
They're hard to pull off, right?

00:48:00.420 --> 00:48:03.480
Ever since what happened last year,

00:48:03.480 --> 00:48:05.730
I've been hoping I'd just play well enough

00:48:06.190 --> 00:48:09.870
that there wouldn't be any more conflict.

00:48:11.510 --> 00:48:12.740
But...

00:48:12.740 --> 00:48:14.740
I'm a third-year.

00:48:15.640 --> 00:48:17.740
This is my last chance.

00:48:18.880 --> 00:48:19.700
Yeah.

00:48:19.700 --> 00:48:21.970
I've been doing this for three years.

00:48:21.970 --> 00:48:23.670
I want to play.

00:48:24.200 --> 00:48:27.630
I want to be able to play
my favorite parts really well.

00:48:34.380 --> 00:48:35.650
Kousaka-san.

00:48:35.650 --> 00:48:36.850
Good morning.

00:48:40.270 --> 00:48:41.430
Practicing?

00:48:41.910 --> 00:48:42.890
Yes.

00:48:42.890 --> 00:48:44.400
Good luck.

00:48:45.060 --> 00:48:46.620
Thank you.

00:49:15.040 --> 00:49:16.440
That sounds good.

00:49:16.440 --> 00:49:17.760
Is that Asuka-senpai?

00:49:22.570 --> 00:49:24.020
Natsuki-senpai?

00:49:41.070 --> 00:49:42.410
<i>Everyone wants to play!</i>

00:49:43.200 --> 00:49:44.920
<i>Everyone wants to be a part of the competition.</i>

00:49:45.760 --> 00:49:49.480
<i>It took me this long to figure out something so obvious.</i>

00:49:50.760 --> 00:49:57.510
<i>It was then that the fear of having to compete against my seniors began to sink in.</i>

00:49:58.830 --> 00:50:01.510
We'll now begin the auditions.

00:50:02.470 --> 00:50:05.270
The A-group competition,
which we're participating in,

00:50:05.270 --> 00:50:09.780
allows a maximum of fifty-five members per ensemble.

00:50:10.270 --> 00:50:15.410
In other words, some of you here will not be participating.

00:50:15.410 --> 00:50:17.760
Everyone, are you nervous?

00:50:17.760 --> 00:50:19.980
Totally nervous!

00:50:19.980 --> 00:50:21.030
Of course you are.

00:50:21.530 --> 00:50:27.240
But I believe all of you here deserve to be in the competition.

00:50:27.240 --> 00:50:28.750
You've all worked very hard.

00:50:29.580 --> 00:50:33.550
Please stand tall and show me the fruits of your efforts.

00:50:34.050 --> 00:50:36.010
Let's begin.

00:50:36.010 --> 00:50:38.050
Thank you!

00:50:44.650 --> 00:50:46.490
Are you already in tune?

00:50:46.490 --> 00:50:47.790
Yes.

00:50:53.260 --> 00:50:55.070
And you're fine with the chair facing that direction?

00:50:55.720 --> 00:50:57.070
I'm fine.

00:50:57.070 --> 00:50:59.500
Let's begin, then.

00:50:59.500 --> 00:51:02.580
Euphoniums come in at bar 23, correct?

00:51:02.580 --> 00:51:03.650
Yes.

00:51:23.810 --> 00:51:29.150
<i>I couldn't tell whether my turn was long or short.</i>

00:51:31.570 --> 00:51:37.190
<i>With my heart still on the verge of exploding from the excitement and anxiety</i>

00:51:37.190 --> 00:51:39.590
<i>I left the music room.</i>

00:51:43.170 --> 00:51:47.700
<i>A few days passed before the results were announced.</i>

00:51:48.670 --> 00:51:50.790
<i>The jitters from the auditions came back,</i>

00:51:51.530 --> 00:51:54.400
<i>and the tension was so thick, you could cut it with a knife. </i>

00:51:55.580 --> 00:51:58.640
I will now announce those
who have passed auditions.

00:51:58.640 --> 00:52:00.770
Respond with "Yes"
when your name is called.

00:52:00.770 --> 00:52:01.680
Okay!

00:52:02.050 --> 00:52:03.390
First, percussion.

00:52:03.390 --> 00:52:04.450
Tanabe Narai.

00:52:04.450 --> 00:52:05.060
Yes.

00:52:05.060 --> 00:52:06.110
Kayama Saki.

00:52:06.110 --> 00:52:06.540
Yes.

00:52:06.540 --> 00:52:07.700
Takashita Chieri.

00:52:07.700 --> 00:52:08.370
Yes.

00:52:08.370 --> 00:52:10.210
Total, eleven clarinets.

00:52:10.210 --> 00:52:11.440
Takigawa Chikao.

00:52:11.440 --> 00:52:12.290
Yes.

00:52:12.290 --> 00:52:14.160
Total, seven saxophones.

00:52:15.570 --> 00:52:17.440
Next, euphonium.

00:52:17.440 --> 00:52:18.610
Tanaka Asuka.

00:52:18.970 --> 00:52:19.780
Yes.

00:52:19.780 --> 00:52:21.320
Oumae Kumiko.

00:52:21.320 --> 00:52:22.260
Yes.

00:52:22.260 --> 00:52:23.530
Total, two.

00:52:25.300 --> 00:52:26.760
Next, tuba.

00:52:26.760 --> 00:52:27.940
Gotou Takuya.

00:52:27.940 --> 00:52:28.450
Yes.

00:52:28.970 --> 00:52:30.080
Nagase Riko.

00:52:30.080 --> 00:52:30.930
Yes.

00:52:30.930 --> 00:52:32.130
Total, two.

00:52:32.700 --> 00:52:34.340
Next, contrabass.

00:52:34.340 --> 00:52:35.690
Kawashima Sapphire.

00:52:35.690 --> 00:52:36.090
Yes.

00:52:38.200 --> 00:52:40.670
Finally, trumpets.

00:52:41.080 --> 00:52:42.480
Nakaseko Kaori.

00:52:42.480 --> 00:52:43.180
Yes.

00:52:43.650 --> 00:52:44.800
Kasano Sana.

00:52:44.800 --> 00:52:45.740
Yes.

00:52:45.740 --> 00:52:46.850
Takino Junichi.

00:52:46.850 --> 00:52:47.520
Yes.

00:52:47.520 --> 00:52:48.740
Yoshikawa Yuuko.

00:52:48.740 --> 00:52:49.430
Yes.

00:52:49.800 --> 00:52:51.300
Kousaka Reina.

00:52:51.300 --> 00:52:51.940
Yes.

00:52:51.940 --> 00:52:53.920
Total, five.

00:52:53.920 --> 00:52:56.190
Kousaka Reina will be playing the solo parts.

00:53:05.280 --> 00:53:06.090
Yes.

00:53:20.000 --> 00:53:22.160
Three minutes, twenty-five seconds.

00:53:22.160 --> 00:53:24.760
I think that tempo was good for the required piece.

00:53:25.390 --> 00:53:27.920
In the competition, performances are limited to twelve minutes.

00:53:27.920 --> 00:53:30.520
So it goes without saying that we can't exceed that.

00:53:30.520 --> 00:53:34.270
But on the flipside, we can't let ourselves ruin the piece by rushing through it.

00:53:34.650 --> 00:53:37.360
Let's not forget that pace.

00:53:37.360 --> 00:53:39.700
If we stick to it, we'll be done well within time.

00:53:39.700 --> 00:53:40.530
Okay.

00:53:40.530 --> 00:53:43.040
Let's call it a day.

00:53:43.040 --> 00:53:44.780
Thank you very much!

00:53:47.050 --> 00:53:49.780
Jeez, do something about that habit of yours!

00:53:49.780 --> 00:53:52.770
I'm having trouble with this part.

00:53:52.770 --> 00:53:55.290
That's probably because it's where
there's a really sudden tempo change.

00:53:55.290 --> 00:53:56.240
Kaori?

00:53:56.880 --> 00:53:57.730
Coming.

00:53:57.730 --> 00:53:58.540
Talk to you later.

00:54:01.280 --> 00:54:02.340
Good work.

00:54:02.340 --> 00:54:04.350
R-Right.

00:54:04.350 --> 00:54:05.380
Good work.

00:54:12.250 --> 00:54:13.640
<i>Kaori-senpai?</i>

00:54:14.950 --> 00:54:17.060
Kousaka? The trumpet player?

00:54:17.060 --> 00:54:19.520
Yes, I overheard them.

00:54:19.520 --> 00:54:21.710
Huh, I had no idea.

00:54:26.630 --> 00:54:32.790
But, like, Taki-sensei isn't the type to, like,
play favorites for a part.

00:54:32.790 --> 00:54:38.630
There's a rumor that the audition was a set-up
so Kousaka-san could play the solo.

00:54:38.630 --> 00:54:43.030
Isn't Kousaka-san's dad
a pretty famous trumpet player?

00:54:43.030 --> 00:54:45.840
There's no way that
Taki-sensei could refuse, then.

00:54:49.970 --> 00:54:51.460
We're done laying down the blankets.

00:54:51.460 --> 00:54:53.140
Okay, good job.

00:54:54.250 --> 00:54:57.480
The blankets will dampen the sound,

00:54:57.480 --> 00:54:59.700
making the room less reverberant.

00:54:59.700 --> 00:55:04.830
To get your sound to travel, you'll need to play stronger and more accurately.

00:55:05.860 --> 00:55:10.350
The venue will be several dozen times bigger than this room.

00:55:10.350 --> 00:55:15.280
Keep that in mind at all times
during our rehearsals.

00:55:15.280 --> 00:55:16.040
Okay.

00:55:16.400 --> 00:55:18.890
Then, everyone, let's begin practice.

00:55:18.890 --> 00:55:20.020
Yes.

00:55:20.020 --> 00:55:21.000
Taki-sensei!

00:55:21.510 --> 00:55:24.340
I have a question. May I?

00:55:24.340 --> 00:55:25.260
What is it?

00:55:27.290 --> 00:55:31.920
Is it true that you knew Kousaka Reina-san
before coming to this school?

00:55:33.230 --> 00:55:35.390
What do you hope to achieve by asking me that?

00:55:35.390 --> 00:55:36.760
Yuuko-chan, no!

00:55:36.760 --> 00:55:41.620
There's a rumor that you were playing favorites
when you were judging auditions.

00:55:41.620 --> 00:55:43.550
Tell us the truth!

00:55:43.550 --> 00:55:47.650
I never played favorites
or treated anyone differently.

00:55:48.070 --> 00:55:49.870
I evaluated everyone fairly.

00:55:49.870 --> 00:55:52.120
And about you having known Kousaka-san?

00:55:55.370 --> 00:55:56.510
That's true.

00:55:57.420 --> 00:56:00.080
Our fathers were acquainted.

00:56:00.080 --> 00:56:02.690
I've known her since she was in middle school.

00:56:03.900 --> 00:56:05.680
Why didn't you tell us?

00:56:05.680 --> 00:56:07.750
I didn't see a reason to.

00:56:07.750 --> 00:56:10.480
It doesn't make any difference in my teaching.

00:56:10.480 --> 00:56:11.190
Then—

00:56:11.190 --> 00:56:12.590
Then what?

00:56:13.130 --> 00:56:15.310
Please don't try to insult him.

00:56:15.550 --> 00:56:18.520
You know <i>exactly</i> why I was chosen.

00:56:18.520 --> 00:56:21.270
It's because I'm better than Kaori-senpai!

00:56:22.200 --> 00:56:25.270
Seriously, you're way too full of yourself!

00:56:25.270 --> 00:56:26.360
Yuuko-chan, don't!

00:56:26.360 --> 00:56:30.070
Do you have any idea how kind Kaori-senpai has been to you?!

00:56:30.070 --> 00:56:30.650
And you—

00:56:30.650 --> 00:56:31.420
Stop.

00:56:31.420 --> 00:56:32.160
Shut up!

00:56:32.160 --> 00:56:33.810
Stop!

00:56:35.930 --> 00:56:36.780
Stop...

00:56:39.900 --> 00:56:43.330
If you're going to complain,
do it when you've surpassed me.

00:56:48.850 --> 00:56:49.840
Reina!

00:56:49.840 --> 00:56:51.470
Kumiko-chan...

00:56:51.470 --> 00:56:53.590
Continue setting up.

00:56:53.990 --> 00:56:55.850
Let's begin rehearsal.

00:56:55.850 --> 00:56:58.580
Reina. Reina!

00:56:58.580 --> 00:56:59.310
I can't stand her.

00:57:00.060 --> 00:57:01.120
Huh?

00:57:03.980 --> 00:57:05.730
I can't stand her. I can't stand her!

00:57:05.730 --> 00:57:08.230
God <i>damn</i>, what is her problem?!

00:57:08.570 --> 00:57:10.900
She can hardly even play! What's wrong with her?!

00:57:09.130 --> 00:57:10.230
Reina...

00:57:10.900 --> 00:57:12.110
Don't you think so?!

00:57:13.350 --> 00:57:14.700
Why are you laughing?

00:57:14.700 --> 00:57:18.030
Sorry, I totally thought you were depressed—

00:57:18.890 --> 00:57:20.060
Kumiko.

00:57:20.060 --> 00:57:21.870
What is it?

00:57:22.430 --> 00:57:24.330
Do you think I'm wrong?

00:57:25.640 --> 00:57:26.710
No.

00:57:27.390 --> 00:57:28.670
I don't.

00:57:28.670 --> 00:57:30.200
Really?

00:57:30.200 --> 00:57:31.130
Yeah.

00:57:35.750 --> 00:57:40.010
I like Taki-sensei.

00:57:41.200 --> 00:57:43.250
Not a high school crush kind of "like" either.

00:57:43.250 --> 00:57:44.440
I mean, I am in love with him.

00:57:46.480 --> 00:57:47.150
Love?

00:57:47.150 --> 00:57:49.380
Don't repeat it! You're embarrassing me.

00:57:49.380 --> 00:57:50.630
Sorry.

00:57:50.630 --> 00:57:54.870
But Taki-sensei doesn't know how I feel.

00:57:54.870 --> 00:57:56.990
He'd never favor me in the audition.

00:57:57.570 --> 00:58:01.500
I can't believe she'd start complaining about our advisor at a time like this.

00:58:02.460 --> 00:58:03.500
Same.

00:58:03.500 --> 00:58:04.780
Why are you looking at me like that?

00:58:04.780 --> 00:58:08.290
Nothing, I was just thinking that you're cute.

00:58:08.290 --> 00:58:09.460
You're terrible.

00:58:12.410 --> 00:58:13.820
Would you ever give up your solo?

00:58:13.820 --> 00:58:14.420
Never.

00:58:14.690 --> 00:58:16.020
I'd double down on it.

00:58:16.020 --> 00:58:18.590
That's what it takes to become special.

00:58:20.280 --> 00:58:21.970
That's so you.

00:58:23.110 --> 00:58:27.150
<i>But at the time, it might not have been clear</i>

00:58:27.800 --> 00:58:31.990
<i>how much effort it takes to try to be strong,</i>

00:58:31.990 --> 00:58:34.240
<i>and to try to become special.</i>

00:58:36.560 --> 00:58:38.240
It's the solo part.

00:58:40.130 --> 00:58:41.700
Caught you peeping!

00:58:43.210 --> 00:58:44.560
Asuka-senpai!

00:58:44.560 --> 00:58:45.370
Did you wet yourself?

00:58:47.450 --> 00:58:50.990
Of course you'd be the one sniffing out the good stuff.

00:58:50.990 --> 00:58:52.820
Sniffing out?

00:58:52.820 --> 00:58:55.630
I just happened to be passing by.

00:58:57.400 --> 00:59:00.230
Looks like she hasn't given up.

00:59:00.230 --> 00:59:01.850
You mean Kaori-senpai?

00:59:02.170 --> 00:59:04.810
It isn't that she has a problem with the audition results.

00:59:04.810 --> 00:59:08.500
She definitely isn't trying to win any sympathy votes, either.

00:59:08.500 --> 00:59:11.770
I guess it's just <i>herself that she can't accept.</i>

00:59:11.770 --> 00:59:13.180
Accept?

00:59:13.180 --> 00:59:15.740
Yeah, she wants to accept herself.

00:59:16.820 --> 00:59:19.360
What do you think, Asuka-senpai?

00:59:19.360 --> 00:59:20.660
About what?

00:59:20.660 --> 00:59:22.370
About the audition.

00:59:22.370 --> 00:59:27.080
Between Kaori-senpai and Reina,
who do you think should play the solo?

00:59:27.080 --> 00:59:29.420
I don't think I can answer that.

00:59:29.420 --> 00:59:31.790
After all, I'm the vice president.

00:59:31.790 --> 00:59:33.920
No personal comments!

00:59:34.500 --> 00:59:37.840
Then tell me, off the record.

00:59:37.840 --> 00:59:38.760
Tell you what?

00:59:38.760 --> 00:59:41.220
What you think, personally.

00:59:42.880 --> 00:59:45.180
You sure are interesting, Oumae-chan.

00:59:45.480 --> 00:59:47.040
Can you keep it a secret?

00:59:47.040 --> 00:59:48.140
I'll do my best.

00:59:48.540 --> 00:59:50.070
You're honest.

00:59:51.440 --> 00:59:56.170
Frankly, I genuinely don't care.

00:59:56.170 --> 00:59:59.360
I don't give a damn who plays a solo or whatever.

01:00:01.210 --> 01:00:04.080
<i>I didn't know if she meant it, or if it was a facade.</i>

01:00:04.080 --> 01:00:08.370
<i>Asuka-senpai's disguise was too thick to see through.</i>

01:00:08.370 --> 01:00:12.000
<i>There was no way I'd be able to rip it off.</i>

01:00:14.740 --> 01:00:18.670
Okay, um, I think Taki-sensei's coming soon.

01:00:19.030 --> 01:00:21.310
There's something I want to talk to you about first.

01:00:21.760 --> 01:00:23.120
So I was thinking, Lala—

01:00:23.120 --> 01:00:24.560
Hitomi-san, listen up.

01:00:25.390 --> 01:00:26.100
Okay.

01:00:27.260 --> 01:00:31.560
I've heard completely baseless rumors about our teacher a lot lately.

01:00:32.040 --> 01:00:34.400
We're all losing focus because of it.

01:00:34.400 --> 01:00:35.890
The competition's coming up.

01:00:35.890 --> 01:00:40.030
At this rate, I'm not sure
we can get silver, let alone gold.

01:00:40.410 --> 01:00:43.100
Just because he knew some students

01:00:43.100 --> 01:00:45.990
doesn't mean there was
any wrongdoing in the audition process.

01:00:45.990 --> 01:00:48.020
If you still have a problem with it,

01:00:48.020 --> 01:00:49.650
don't whisper about it
behind everyone's backs.

01:00:49.650 --> 01:00:51.520
A show of hands, please.

01:00:51.520 --> 01:00:53.460
I'll tell Taki-sensei myself.

01:00:54.460 --> 01:00:56.210
Who has a problem with the results of the auditions?

01:01:06.360 --> 01:01:07.080
Okay.

01:01:08.750 --> 01:01:09.990
Taki-sensei!

01:01:09.990 --> 01:01:12.590
You're all quiet today.

01:01:13.290 --> 01:01:14.060
Why the hands?

01:01:14.060 --> 01:01:16.800
We have a problem with the audition results.

01:01:16.800 --> 01:01:17.970
Yuuko-chan!

01:01:19.030 --> 01:01:20.380
I understand.

01:01:20.380 --> 01:01:22.780
First, I have an announcement to make.

01:01:24.090 --> 01:01:28.340
I've told you that we've rented a hall to practice in, correct?

01:01:28.950 --> 01:01:34.830
While we're there, I'd like to offer a second round of auditions to anyone interested.

01:01:35.920 --> 01:01:38.290
If you weren't happy with the last audition

01:01:38.660 --> 01:01:42.300
and you would like to try again, please raise your hand now.

01:01:42.870 --> 01:01:45.480
You'll play in front of the whole ensemble next week,

01:01:45.480 --> 01:01:48.640
and we'll decide based on a count of hands.

01:01:48.640 --> 01:01:51.020
We'll all decide together.

01:01:51.020 --> 01:01:53.120
That will leave no room for objections.

01:01:53.120 --> 01:01:54.060
Understood?

01:01:56.810 --> 01:01:58.310
I'll ask again.

01:01:59.000 --> 01:02:01.290
Who would like another audition?

01:02:13.190 --> 01:02:17.500
Please let me redo the audition for the solo part.

01:02:18.670 --> 01:02:20.210
Kaori...

01:02:20.210 --> 01:02:21.500
All right.

01:02:22.380 --> 01:02:26.970
Since Kousaka-san is the current soloist,

01:02:27.340 --> 01:02:31.720
you and Kousaka-san will have
a second audition for the solo part.

01:02:46.950 --> 01:02:48.160
Good morning.

01:02:54.710 --> 01:02:55.740
Good morning.

01:03:06.300 --> 01:03:07.660
What's wrong?

01:03:07.660 --> 01:03:08.470
Huh?

01:03:11.800 --> 01:03:15.310
Oh, nothing.

01:03:16.180 --> 01:03:17.030
I see.

01:03:32.290 --> 01:03:33.700
Sorry to call you out here.

01:03:33.700 --> 01:03:34.870
It's fine.

01:03:35.260 --> 01:03:37.570
What did you want to talk about?

01:03:37.570 --> 01:03:38.460
Reina...

01:03:41.230 --> 01:03:43.690
Is it about the audition?

01:03:43.690 --> 01:03:44.420
Yeah.

01:03:49.360 --> 01:03:53.000
We have to be there by eight.

01:03:53.000 --> 01:03:54.040
Yeah.

01:03:54.040 --> 01:03:55.090
You know...

01:03:55.090 --> 01:03:55.720
Yes?

01:03:57.090 --> 01:03:58.660
I really,

01:03:59.190 --> 01:04:02.510
<i>really</i> want Kaori-senpai to play the solo.

01:04:03.480 --> 01:04:06.190
So, please!

01:04:10.890 --> 01:04:13.030
Are you asking me to throw the audition?

01:04:16.210 --> 01:04:19.020
If anyone finds out, you can tell them I threatened you.

01:04:19.020 --> 01:04:21.740
I don't mind if you tell them I bullied you.

01:04:21.740 --> 01:04:22.830
So...

01:04:22.830 --> 01:04:25.200
There's no need for any of that.

01:04:25.200 --> 01:04:28.820
Kaori-senpai simply has to play better than I do at the audition.

01:04:29.720 --> 01:04:31.070
I know that.

01:04:32.620 --> 01:04:36.720
Last year, Kaori-senpai was the best player in the entire ensemble.

01:04:37.470 --> 01:04:39.350
But parts were handed out based on seniority,

01:04:39.350 --> 01:04:43.250
so an upperclassman got the solo parts,
even though she'd hardly ever practiced.

01:04:45.270 --> 01:04:50.350
Not only that, Kaori-senpai even tried to resign from the competition

01:04:50.350 --> 01:04:53.040
to stop the first-years from quitting.

01:04:54.220 --> 01:04:56.460
But they quit anyway.

01:04:56.460 --> 01:05:00.410
Our performance at the competition was a wreck.

01:05:00.770 --> 01:05:02.250
That's got nothing to do with me.

01:05:03.100 --> 01:05:05.460
That's got nothing to do with me, right?

01:05:05.820 --> 01:05:07.860
You're right, it doesn't.

01:05:07.860 --> 01:05:09.590
Not one bit.

01:05:09.590 --> 01:05:12.060
But you have next year.

01:05:12.060 --> 01:05:13.700
And the year after that!

01:05:13.700 --> 01:05:15.930
Taki-sensei will make the band even better.

01:05:16.640 --> 01:05:18.140
But this is Kaori-senpai's last chance.

01:05:18.670 --> 01:05:21.010
This year is her last year!

01:05:21.010 --> 01:05:22.350
So...

01:05:23.540 --> 01:05:24.940
Please don't.

01:05:26.910 --> 01:05:28.340
Excuse me.

01:05:46.210 --> 01:05:48.160
This place is huge!

01:05:48.160 --> 01:05:51.370
The competition will take place in an even larger hall.

01:05:51.370 --> 01:05:54.130
If this is enough to stun you,
you'll be overwhelmed at the competition.

01:05:58.040 --> 01:05:59.140
How are you doing?

01:06:00.520 --> 01:06:01.970
I'm good.

01:06:01.970 --> 01:06:04.770
The ensemble needs to set up.
You should go help, Yuuko-chan.

01:06:06.130 --> 01:06:07.060
Okay.

01:06:11.500 --> 01:06:12.110
Hey...

01:06:15.900 --> 01:06:16.530
Yes?

01:06:17.950 --> 01:06:18.720
Nothing.

01:06:19.480 --> 01:06:20.880
Good luck!

01:06:30.170 --> 01:06:30.960
What is it?

01:06:42.570 --> 01:06:45.230
We're almost done setting up.

01:06:45.230 --> 01:06:46.160
Yeah?

01:06:47.330 --> 01:06:48.610
Are you okay?

01:06:49.240 --> 01:06:49.950
Yeah.

01:06:55.710 --> 01:06:56.860
Kumiko.

01:06:58.770 --> 01:07:00.080
Would you...

01:07:01.270 --> 01:07:05.150
be upset if I lost?

01:07:06.120 --> 01:07:07.330
Reina...

01:07:12.570 --> 01:07:13.500
I would.

01:07:14.880 --> 01:07:16.000
I would!

01:07:16.650 --> 01:07:17.340
Why?

01:07:17.610 --> 01:07:19.800
You're going to become
someone special, aren't you?

01:07:20.870 --> 01:07:22.070
Right.

01:07:22.070 --> 01:07:24.600
You're different from the others.

01:07:25.410 --> 01:07:27.670
You're different from everyone else!

01:07:27.670 --> 01:07:29.920
You can't let yourself be influenced by others!

01:07:30.820 --> 01:07:32.560
That'd be plain stupid!

01:07:32.560 --> 01:07:33.650
But...

01:07:34.360 --> 01:07:36.780
if I win now, I'll be the villain.

01:07:36.780 --> 01:07:37.920
Whatever!

01:07:37.920 --> 01:07:40.980
When that happens,
I'll be a villain with you.

01:07:40.980 --> 01:07:44.080
You're better than Kaori-senpai.

01:07:44.080 --> 01:07:46.750
I'll tell them it ought to be you to play the solo.

01:07:46.750 --> 01:07:47.790
I'll tell them!

01:07:48.120 --> 01:07:48.870
Really?

01:07:51.520 --> 01:07:52.840
Probably.

01:07:54.520 --> 01:07:57.050
You sure are a terrible person.

01:08:04.200 --> 01:08:05.820
Will you stay with me?

01:08:05.820 --> 01:08:06.550
Yeah.

01:08:07.250 --> 01:08:08.820
You won't abandon me?

01:08:08.820 --> 01:08:11.240
If I do, you can kill me.

01:08:11.880 --> 01:08:13.810
I actually <i>would</i> kill you.

01:08:13.810 --> 01:08:15.990
Knowing you, I don't doubt that for a moment.

01:08:15.990 --> 01:08:18.000
I'm prepared for that.

01:08:18.650 --> 01:08:22.360
This is a confession of love, after all.

01:08:31.740 --> 01:08:32.580
Reina.

01:08:36.250 --> 01:08:38.000
Don't worry.

01:08:38.000 --> 01:08:41.430
I never had any intention of losing to begin with.

01:08:49.930 --> 01:08:55.110
Let's begin the audition for the trumpet solo.

01:08:55.850 --> 01:08:57.570
Once they're both done playing,

01:08:57.570 --> 01:09:00.070
we'll all decide together, based on applause.

01:09:00.070 --> 01:09:02.320
Understand, Nakaseko-san?

01:09:02.320 --> 01:09:03.320
Yes.

01:09:03.320 --> 01:09:04.450
Kousaka-san?

01:09:04.450 --> 01:09:05.450
Yes.

01:09:06.220 --> 01:09:10.190
Okay then, Nakaseko-san, please.

01:09:10.190 --> 01:09:11.010
Yes.

01:10:09.290 --> 01:10:11.200
Thank you.

01:10:26.280 --> 01:10:29.910
Next, Kousaka-san, please.

01:10:30.180 --> 01:10:31.210
Yes.

01:11:41.340 --> 01:11:42.950
Thank you.

01:11:47.770 --> 01:11:51.240
I'd like for us to choose the soloist now.

01:11:51.800 --> 01:11:53.740
Who thinks Nakaseko-san should play?

01:12:05.340 --> 01:12:06.160
Okay.

01:12:08.470 --> 01:12:11.840
Now, who thinks Kousaka-san should play?

01:12:22.920 --> 01:12:23.750
Okay.

01:12:26.440 --> 01:12:27.530
Nakaseko-san?

01:12:28.040 --> 01:12:29.030
Yes?

01:12:30.120 --> 01:12:32.280
Will you play the solo?

01:12:49.500 --> 01:12:50.820
I won't.

01:12:53.280 --> 01:12:54.580
I can't.

01:12:57.710 --> 01:12:58.990
Kaori-senpai...

01:12:58.990 --> 01:13:00.060
I think...

01:13:00.580 --> 01:13:03.080
that Kousaka-san should play the solo.

01:13:10.480 --> 01:13:12.030
Kaori-senpai!

01:13:12.110 --> 01:13:15.700
You're so good at playing the trumpet!

01:13:16.790 --> 01:13:18.290
Not really.

01:13:18.980 --> 01:13:20.250
I just enjoy it.

01:13:32.490 --> 01:13:33.430
Kousaka-san.

01:13:33.760 --> 01:13:34.870
Yes?

01:13:34.870 --> 01:13:36.180
You will be playing the solo.

01:13:36.660 --> 01:13:38.180
Not Nakaseko-san.

01:13:38.580 --> 01:13:40.100
You'll play.

01:13:40.840 --> 01:13:41.680
Understood?

01:13:43.020 --> 01:13:43.740
Yes.

01:13:59.850 --> 01:14:03.940
<i>The intensity and passion in practicing
for the competition grew ever higher and hotter.</i>

01:14:03.940 --> 01:14:06.240
<i>The ensemble was absorbed with musical achievement,</i>

01:14:06.240 --> 01:14:09.410
<i>its former self from spring
long lost in the flames.</i>

01:14:15.440 --> 01:14:16.930
Okay, that's enough.

01:14:18.370 --> 01:14:21.470
Trombones, which of you missed your entrance?

01:14:23.050 --> 01:14:26.710
If you can't do it during rehearsal,
you'll never do it in a performance.

01:14:26.710 --> 01:14:28.560
Please keep that in mind.

01:14:28.560 --> 01:14:29.940
Yes.

01:14:29.940 --> 01:14:32.860
Okay, from measure 158.

01:14:46.010 --> 01:14:47.500
Okay, stop.

01:14:49.140 --> 01:14:53.710
Euphoniums, can I hear you
one at a time, starting at 162?

01:14:53.710 --> 01:14:54.630
Beginning with Oumae-san.

01:14:54.630 --> 01:14:56.260
Y-Yes.

01:15:05.520 --> 01:15:07.210
Okay, enough.

01:15:09.520 --> 01:15:11.900
Oumae-san, is that part too difficult for you?

01:15:13.740 --> 01:15:16.400
Will you be able to play it by the performance?

01:15:16.400 --> 01:15:17.300
Yes.

01:15:17.300 --> 01:15:21.790
If you can't play it at the performance, you'll be causing trouble for everyone.

01:15:22.590 --> 01:15:24.130
I'll ask you again.

01:15:24.130 --> 01:15:25.330
Will you be able to play it?

01:15:26.250 --> 01:15:27.580
Yes, I will!

01:15:29.210 --> 01:15:30.580
Very well.

01:15:30.970 --> 01:15:33.090
Okay, all together, starting at the next part.

01:15:36.700 --> 01:15:40.690
<i>The fingerings as well as the strength and timings of my breaths...</i>

01:15:40.690 --> 01:15:43.310
<i>Imagining the sound is no problem.</i>

01:15:43.310 --> 01:15:46.060
<i>But the frustration of being unable to reproduce it...</i>

01:15:47.010 --> 01:15:50.730
<i>I was confronted by the difficulty of producing each note,</i>

01:15:50.730 --> 01:15:52.660
<i>one after another,</i>

01:15:52.660 --> 01:15:56.570
<i>with exactly the right amount of force,</i>

01:15:57.610 --> 01:16:00.200
<i>strength of breath, tone, and rhythm.</i>

01:16:03.200 --> 01:16:04.810
Let's begin.

01:16:04.810 --> 01:16:06.410
Measure 158.

01:16:25.610 --> 01:16:27.100
Okay, stop.

01:16:28.060 --> 01:16:30.560
Trumpets, be sure to end your notes cleanly.

01:16:30.560 --> 01:16:31.310
Yes.

01:16:31.670 --> 01:16:33.060
More out of the horns, please.

01:16:33.060 --> 01:16:33.810
Yes.

01:16:34.150 --> 01:16:38.320
And euphs, I'd like Tanaka-san
to play this part alone.

01:16:40.860 --> 01:16:42.950
Tanaka-san, did you hear me?

01:16:43.480 --> 01:16:44.290
Yes.

01:16:45.230 --> 01:16:46.210
Once more.

01:16:46.210 --> 01:16:48.770
Pay attention to what I just told you.

01:16:48.770 --> 01:16:49.550
Three...

01:16:54.770 --> 01:16:56.960
<i>It happened in an instant.</i>

01:16:56.960 --> 01:16:59.230
<i>I didn't even get the chance to argue.</i>

01:16:59.230 --> 01:17:02.470
<i>That was all he said before we went straight back to rehearsing.</i>

01:17:05.350 --> 01:17:10.040
<i>Indeed... We were at war to make it
to the Kansai Competition.</i>

01:17:20.320 --> 01:17:21.990
<i>I... want to improve.</i>

01:17:23.340 --> 01:17:24.960
<i>I want to improve.</i>

01:17:28.880 --> 01:17:30.830
<i>I want to improve.</i>

01:17:32.580 --> 01:17:34.860
<i>I want to improve!</i>

01:17:34.860 --> 01:17:36.590
<i>I want to improve!</i>

01:17:37.050 --> 01:17:38.770
<i>I want to improve!</i>

01:17:39.460 --> 01:17:42.010
<i>I want to be better than everyone!</i>

01:17:42.010 --> 01:17:42.670
<i>Everyone...</i>

01:17:53.750 --> 01:17:58.730
I want to improve!

01:17:59.980 --> 01:18:01.710
Hey, Kumiko!

01:18:01.710 --> 01:18:03.370
What's up?

01:18:04.170 --> 01:18:05.960
I want to improve.

01:18:05.960 --> 01:18:07.080
What?

01:18:08.350 --> 01:18:10.490
I said that I want to improve!

01:18:11.500 --> 01:18:15.500
So do I. I want to improve too!

01:18:15.500 --> 01:18:17.950
I want to improve more!

01:18:17.950 --> 01:18:20.340
No, <i>I</i> want to improve more!

01:18:20.790 --> 01:18:22.420
I...

01:18:29.880 --> 01:18:31.370
I hate this!

01:18:34.470 --> 01:18:37.250
I hate this so much, I want to die.

01:18:48.340 --> 01:18:50.620
<i>That's when I realized...</i>

01:18:51.180 --> 01:18:53.230
<i>I hate this so much, I want to die.</i>

01:18:54.360 --> 01:18:55.750
<i>...how much it hurts.</i>

01:18:56.090 --> 01:18:57.460
Because I'm upset!

01:18:57.460 --> 01:19:03.630
<i>I understood how Reina felt back then.</i>

01:18:57.920 --> 01:18:59.760
I'm totally upset!

01:19:15.420 --> 01:19:16.480
Oumae-san?

01:19:16.780 --> 01:19:19.230
What brings you here so late?

01:19:19.560 --> 01:19:22.640
Sorry, I forgot something.

01:19:22.640 --> 01:19:24.610
What did you forget?

01:19:26.440 --> 01:19:27.490
My phone.

01:19:28.510 --> 01:19:30.660
I hope you weren't using it during class.

01:19:30.660 --> 01:19:32.250
N-No.

01:19:32.250 --> 01:19:34.060
Please be more careful.

01:19:34.060 --> 01:19:36.760
The vice principal will yell at me again.

01:19:36.760 --> 01:19:37.690
Again?

01:19:37.690 --> 01:19:41.860
Yes, I've been getting scolded a lot lately.

01:19:41.860 --> 01:19:43.680
For making you guys practice too much.

01:19:44.920 --> 01:19:47.730
I don't let it bother me, though.

01:19:50.730 --> 01:19:55.310
Your father is Taki Tooru-san, right?

01:19:55.310 --> 01:19:56.230
Yes.

01:19:56.230 --> 01:19:57.560
I'm surprised you know that.

01:19:58.040 --> 01:20:00.140
Up until ten years ago,

01:20:00.140 --> 01:20:03.380
my father was an advisor to
the wind ensemble at this school.

01:20:03.380 --> 01:20:08.130
So I was pretty happy
when I was assigned to this school.

01:20:08.130 --> 01:20:13.450
Aren't you under a lot of pressure
since you're doing the same job as your father?

01:20:13.450 --> 01:20:15.500
I'm not sure.

01:20:15.500 --> 01:20:20.710
When I was young, I never even thought about having the same job as my father.

01:20:21.200 --> 01:20:23.590
But this was the job I ultimately chose.

01:20:24.050 --> 01:20:27.840
I suppose that's what it's like to have something you enjoy doing.

01:20:29.490 --> 01:20:30.430
Right?

01:20:31.180 --> 01:20:31.760
Sorry?

01:20:35.890 --> 01:20:38.130
Thank you.

01:20:38.130 --> 01:20:39.410
It's late.

01:20:39.410 --> 01:20:41.150
Be sure you get home safely.

01:20:41.150 --> 01:20:41.860
Yes.

01:20:43.300 --> 01:20:45.150
Oh, by the way...

01:20:46.250 --> 01:20:49.400
Practice that part you were
having trouble with, please.

01:20:49.400 --> 01:20:51.400
For the Kansai Competition.

01:20:53.210 --> 01:20:57.540
I haven't forgotten that
you said you could do it.

01:20:59.460 --> 01:21:00.620
Certainly!

01:21:56.760 --> 01:21:57.800
Okay!

01:21:58.200 --> 01:21:59.680
Do you have everything you need?

01:21:59.680 --> 01:22:00.530
Yeah.

01:22:02.500 --> 01:22:03.880
I'm heading out.

01:22:18.200 --> 01:22:19.810
Morning.

01:22:19.810 --> 01:22:20.880
Morning...

01:22:45.860 --> 01:22:47.650
Go, Kitauji!

01:22:47.900 --> 01:22:49.360
Yeah!

01:22:50.830 --> 01:22:53.090
Are you nervous, Kumiko-chan?

01:22:53.090 --> 01:22:54.360
No, I'm not.

01:22:54.360 --> 01:22:55.880
You are.

01:22:55.880 --> 01:23:00.160
Listen, you're nervous because you're worried about failing.

01:23:00.540 --> 01:23:04.120
Just think about showing off your skills.

01:23:04.690 --> 01:23:06.400
You're so strong, Midori-chan.

01:23:06.400 --> 01:23:09.080
I'm just so excited!

01:23:09.630 --> 01:23:11.890
I can't wait to play!

01:23:17.340 --> 01:23:18.680
It's huge.

01:23:18.680 --> 01:23:19.840
Isn't it?

01:23:30.760 --> 01:23:31.530
It's Rikka.

01:23:31.530 --> 01:23:33.520
There are so many of them.

01:23:33.520 --> 01:23:36.650
Okay, everyone, gather around over here.

01:23:41.320 --> 01:23:44.330
Instrument movers, let's get going!

01:23:44.330 --> 01:23:45.330
Okay.

01:23:45.330 --> 01:23:46.320
Kumiko.

01:23:49.260 --> 01:23:50.830
Tie my hair up for me.

01:23:53.420 --> 01:23:54.920
As tight as you can.

01:23:54.920 --> 01:23:56.460
Got it.

01:24:06.740 --> 01:24:07.430
Oumae-chan.

01:24:17.260 --> 01:24:20.910
You're free to play as long as this door is closed.

01:24:38.050 --> 01:24:39.520
I'm out of tune.

01:24:39.520 --> 01:24:41.490
It's okay. Stay calm.

01:24:41.490 --> 01:24:42.730
Here, listen.

01:24:46.090 --> 01:24:47.600
I think you're a bit sharp.

01:25:25.970 --> 01:25:27.370
Are we good?

01:25:27.370 --> 01:25:28.480
Yes.

01:25:28.480 --> 01:25:29.740
Let's see...

01:25:31.990 --> 01:25:36.650
You know, I've been pondering what I should be saying to you right now.

01:25:37.310 --> 01:25:39.900
But there isn't much for me to say.

01:25:42.060 --> 01:25:46.530
This spring, you decided
you would be going for nationals.

01:25:46.990 --> 01:25:53.040
You all came together and made music through your ambition and hard work.

01:25:53.390 --> 01:25:54.530
Be proud.

01:25:56.410 --> 01:26:00.560
We are the Kitauji High School Wind Ensemble.

01:26:02.100 --> 01:26:04.130
It's almost our turn.

01:26:04.130 --> 01:26:04.800
Everyone...

01:26:06.480 --> 01:26:09.310
Are you ready to amaze the audience?

01:26:12.140 --> 01:26:14.260
Are we back to being how we used to be?

01:26:14.730 --> 01:26:16.730
Let's try that again.

01:26:17.560 --> 01:26:20.370
Are you ready to amaze the audience?

01:26:25.160 --> 01:26:26.250
Yes!

01:26:26.250 --> 01:26:28.120
Okay then, let's go.

01:26:31.160 --> 01:26:32.190
To nationals.

01:26:47.340 --> 01:26:50.220
It's a little sad, isn't it?

01:26:53.660 --> 01:26:57.240
We had so much fun,
and now it's about to end.

01:26:59.950 --> 01:27:02.590
I wish summer could go on forever.

01:27:08.100 --> 01:27:09.680
What are you talking about?

01:27:09.680 --> 01:27:11.580
It isn't over yet.

01:27:12.040 --> 01:27:14.790
We're heading to nationals after this.

01:27:20.050 --> 01:27:21.630
You're right.

01:27:21.980 --> 01:27:25.070
Come to think of it, that <i>is</i> our goal.

01:27:29.150 --> 01:27:33.600
<i>Fifth in the program,
Kitauji High School Wind Ensemble.</i>

01:27:33.600 --> 01:27:36.100
<i>Following Required Piece #4,</i>

01:27:36.100 --> 01:27:40.520
for their free-choice piece, they will play
"Crescent Moon Dance," composed by Horikawa Namie.

01:27:41.080 --> 01:27:43.070
<i>Conducted by Taki Noboru.</i>

01:28:43.020 --> 01:28:45.350
<i>I hope we make it to nationals.</i>

01:28:46.400 --> 01:28:49.820
<i>I've had that wish since middle school.</i>

01:28:50.660 --> 01:28:55.300
<i>But back then, I was only saying it.</i>

01:28:55.720 --> 01:29:00.060
<i>I never thought of actually trying to make it happen.</i>

01:29:00.850 --> 01:29:04.310
<i>I thought that it'd be stupid.</i>

01:29:05.610 --> 01:29:09.320
<i>To get my hopes up, only to embarrass myself.</i>

01:29:10.540 --> 01:29:11.550
<i>But...</i>

01:29:13.190 --> 01:29:15.810
<i>Wishes don't come true
unless you mean it when you make them.</i>

01:29:18.080 --> 01:29:21.330
<i>We're definitely going to nationals!</i>

01:30:34.490 --> 01:30:35.650
Awesome.

01:30:38.460 --> 01:30:39.400
I—

01:30:40.780 --> 01:30:42.260
The basses are up.

01:31:27.000 --> 01:31:28.500
Do we all have our instruments?

01:32:53.710 --> 01:32:55.040
Nakagawa-senpai...

01:33:03.200 --> 01:33:04.720
Rikka, we're on the move.

01:33:04.720 --> 01:33:06.030
Okay.

01:35:33.090 --> 01:35:35.580
I'm so nervous.

01:35:36.660 --> 01:35:39.120
I can't take this tension.

01:35:42.780 --> 01:35:43.710
Here we go!

01:35:56.840 --> 01:35:57.980
Kumiko...

01:36:02.760 --> 01:36:03.900
Gold.

01:36:09.400 --> 01:36:13.740
The schools moving on to
the Kansai Competition are...

01:36:49.450 --> 01:36:52.340
<i>And now, our piece goes on!</i>

